  "interpretation": [
    "The final measured layout took 198 s without the native cache and 140 s with it, versus 210 s for the latest serial baseline. The first candidate was 211 s cold and 139 s warm; all trials are included.",
    "Runner totals rose from 206 s to 295 s cold and 232 s warm in the final layout because dependencies are prepared on two runners. This change optimizes waiting time, not minimum runner consumption.",
    "Cold-run differences are too small relative to runner variability to claim a stable 6% speedup. Native compilation varied from 40 s in the baseline log to 61 s and 49 s in the candidates, and MySQL initialization ranged from 19 s to 36 s.",
    "Core, compiler, dependency declarations, build scripts, build command, workflow and native ABI changes invalidate the executable cache. Cache eviction also requires a rebuild; the warm result is not the time for every source change.",
    "After these measurements, package.json was added to the exact native cache key so changing the npm build entry invalidates it as well. This changes cache identity, not job scheduling, compilation or test coverage."
  ]
